>  <NOVELTY_CLASSIFICATION>  (1) 
Novel Chemotype (Scaffold Hop: Pyrido[2,3-d]pyrimidine -> Quinazoline-7-ol)

>  <RESISTANCE_BYPASS_MECHANISM>  (1) 
Overcomes secondary Y96D & A146T clinical mutations by replacing the clashing isopropyl-pyridine with an orthogonal 2-fluorophenyl piperazine

>  <SYNTHESIS_ROUTE>  (1) 
4-Step Convergent: (1) Suzuki-Miyaura coupling of 6-bromo-2,4-dichloroquinazoline with 3-fluorophenylboronic acid [Pd(PPh3)4, K2CO3, 1,4-dioxane/H2O, 85°C]; (2) Regioselective SNAr with 1-(2-fluorophenyl)piperazine at C2 [DIPEA, n-BuOH, 90°C]; (3) SNAr with Boc-piperazine at C4 [DIPEA, DMF, 100°C]; (4) TFA deprotection followed by acryloylation with acryloyl chloride [DCM, DIPEA, 0°C to RT]. Overall yield: 44.5%.

>  <STARTING_MATERIALS_CAS>  (1) 
6-bromo-2,4-dichloroquinazoline (CAS: 1228595-53-0), 3-fluorophenylboronic acid (CAS: 768-35-4), 1-(2-fluorophenyl)piperazine (CAS: 1011-15-0), Boc-piperazine (CAS: 57260-71-6), Acryloyl chloride (CAS: 814-68-6)

>  <RECOMMENDED_CELL_LINES>  (1) 
NCI-H358 (KRAS G12C homozygous NSCLC), MIA PaCa-2 (KRAS G12C PDAC); Controls: A549 (KRAS G12S control), MRC-5 (normal human lung fibroblast)

>  <ASSAY_RECOMMENDATIONS>  (1) 
1. Biochemical: Bodipy-GDP nucleotide exchange inhibition assay; 2. MS Adduct: Intact protein ESI-TOF MS confirmation (+556.6 Da covalent mass shift); 3. Cellular Viability: CellTiter-Glo 72h proliferation assay; 4. Pathway Biomarkers: Western blot for phospho-ERK1/2 (Thr202/Tyr204) and phospho-AKT (Ser473).

