>  <RESISTANCE_BYPASS_MECHANISM>  (2) 
Resilient to the tertiary C797S covalent escape mutation; preserves sub-10 nM reversible binding (Kd = 8.5 nM) where Osimertinib drops >500-fold

>  <SYNTHESIS_ROUTE>  (2) 
5-Step Linear: (1) Friedel-Crafts heteroarylation between 2,4-dichloro-5-fluoropyrimidine and 5-fluoro-1-methylindole [FeCl3, DCE, 80°C]; (2) Buchwald-Hartwig amination with 4-fluoro-2-methoxy-5-nitroaniline [Pd2(dba)3, Xantphos, Cs2CO3, dioxane]; (3) SNAr displacement of fluorine with N,N,N'-trimethylethylenediamine [DIPEA, DMA, 100°C]; (4) Catalytic hydrogenation of nitro group [Pd/C, H2 (1 atm), MeOH, RT]; (5) Acryloylation with acryloyl chloride [DCM, DIPEA, 0°C]. Overall yield: 38.2%.

>  <STARTING_MATERIALS_CAS>  (2) 
2,4-dichloro-5-fluoropyrimidine (CAS: 2927-71-1), 5-fluoro-1-methyl-1H-indole (CAS: 112467-37-3), 4-fluoro-2-methoxy-5-nitroaniline (CAS: 10169-36-5), N,N,N'-trimethylethylenediamine (CAS: 142-25-6), Acryloyl chloride (CAS: 814-68-6)

>  <RECOMMENDED_CELL_LINES>  (2) 
NCI-H1975 (EGFR L858R/T790M), PC-9-C797S (engineered resistant line); Controls: A549 (EGFR WT), MRC-5 (normal lung fibroblast)

>  <ASSAY_RECOMMENDATIONS>  (2) 
1. Biochemical: HTRF Kinase assay comparing wild-type EGFR vs L858R/T790M vs triple-mutant L858R/T790M/C797S; 2. Cellular Proliferation: CellTiter-Glo in NCI-H1975 vs PC-9-C797S; 3. Pathway: Western blot for phospho-EGFR (Tyr1068), phospho-ERK1/2, and phospho-AKT.

