Substantial Bioisosteric Re-engineering (Imidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine & 2-Fluorophenyl Core)

>  <RESISTANCE_BYPASS_MECHANISM>  (3) 
Achieves >45-fold selectivity over VEGFR2/KDR (Kd = 48.6 nM vs 0.4 nM for ABL1), eliminating arterial occlusive thrombosis that triggers Ponatinib's black-box warning

>  <SYNTHESIS_ROUTE>  (3) 
4-Step Convergent: (1) Iodination of imidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine followed by Sonogashira coupling with ethynyltrimethylsilane [Pd(PPh3)2Cl2, CuI, Et3N, THF]; (2) Desilylation with TBAF in THF to yield 3-ethynylimidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine; (3) HATU-mediated amide coupling of 3-iodo-4-methylbenzoic acid with 4-((4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)methyl)-3-fluoroaniline [DIPEA, DMF]; (4) Sonogashira cross-coupling of terminal alkyne with iodobenzamide [Pd(PPh3)4, CuI, Et3N, DMF, 70°C]. Overall yield: 41.0%.

>  <STARTING_MATERIALS_CAS>  (3) 
Imidazo[1,2-a]pyrazine (CAS: 5049-21-8), Ethynyltrimethylsilane (CAS: 1066-54-2), 3-iodo-4-methylbenzoic acid (CAS: 82998-57-0), 4-((4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)methyl)-3-fluoroaniline (CAS: 1221793-76-1)

>  <RECOMMENDED_CELL_LINES>  (3) 
K562 (CML Ph+), Ba/F3-BCR-ABL1 WT, Ba/F3-BCR-ABL1 T315I; Controls: HUVEC (human umbilical vein endothelial cells), CD34+ normal bone marrow cells

>  <ASSAY_RECOMMENDATIONS>  (3) 
1. Biochemical: LanthaScreen TR-FRET kinase assay against ABL1 WT, ABL1 T315I, and VEGFR2/KDR; 2. Cellular Proliferation: Ba/F3 BCR-ABL1 WT vs T315I viability; 3. Endothelial Safety: HUVEC tube formation and cell viability (confirming absence of vascular toxicity).

