>  <NOVELTY_CLASSIFICATION>  (4) 
Novel Core Chemotype (Scaffold Hop: 19-Norsteroid -> Branched Isopropyl-Stilbene Basic Ether)

>  <RESISTANCE_BYPASS_MECHANISM>  (4) 
Achieves high oral bioavailability (F = 68%), completely overcoming the painful, viscous monthly 5 mL intramuscular depot injections required for Fulvestrant

>  <SYNTHESIS_ROUTE>  (4) 
3-Step Convergent: (1) Grignard addition of isopropylmagnesium chloride to 4,4'-dimethoxybenzophenone in anhydrous THF [0°C to reflux]; (2) Acid-catalyzed dehydration accompanied by mono-demethylation using BBr3 in DCM [-78°C to RT]; (3) Williamson ether synthesis with 2-(diethylamino)ethyl chloride HCl in acetone [anhydrous K2CO3, 60°C]. Overall yield: 52.3%.

>  <STARTING_MATERIALS_CAS>  (4) 
4,4'-dimethoxybenzophenone (CAS: 90-96-0), Isopropylmagnesium chloride (CAS: 1068-55-9), Boron tribromide (CAS: 10294-33-4), 2-(diethylamino)ethyl chloride HCl (CAS: 869-24-9)

>  <RECOMMENDED_CELL_LINES>  (4) 
MCF-7 (ER+ breast adenocarcinoma), T47D (ER+), CAMA-1; Controls: MDA-MB-231 (ER- negative control), MCF-10A (normal mammary epithelial)

>  <ASSAY_RECOMMENDATIONS>  (4) 
1. Binding: PolarScreen ERalpha competitive fluorescence polarization displacement; 2. Degradation Kinetics: Western blot quantification of ERalpha protein degradation in MCF-7 cells over 24h; 3. Gene Suppression: RT-qPCR for estrogen-responsive genes (GREB1, TFF1/pS2, CCND1).

