Replaces oxidation-vulnerable tert-butyl group with a fluorinated core that resists CYP3A4 degradation, tripling microsomal half-life (T1/2 = 78 min) and eliminating Ritonavir booster co-dosing

>  <SYNTHESIS_ROUTE>  (5) 
4-Step Peptide Synthesis: (1) Coupling of (1R,2S,5S)-6,6-dimethyl-3-azabicyclo[3.1.0]hexane-2-carboxylic acid with chiral trifluoroacetyl-amino acid intermediate [HATU, DIPEA, DMF]; (2) Peptide coupling with (2S)-2-amino-3-((3S)-2-oxopyrrolidin-3-yl)propanamide [EDCI, HOBt, DCM]; (3) Burgess reagent-mediated dehydration of primary amide to nitrile warhead [DCM, RT]; (4) Preparative chiral HPLC purification. Overall yield: 34.8%.

>  <STARTING_MATERIALS_CAS>  (5) 
(1R,2S,5S)-6,6-dimethyl-3-azabicyclo[3.1.0]hexane-2-carboxylic acid HCl (CAS: 565456-77-1), Chiral P1 pyrrolidin-2-one intermediate, Burgess reagent (CAS: 29684-56-8)

>  <RECOMMENDED_CELL_LINES>  (5) 
Vero E6 (ATCC CRL-1586), Calu-3 human lung adenocarcinoma; Controls: Primary Human Hepatocytes (PHH), HEK-293 (human embryonic kidney)

>  <ASSAY_RECOMMENDATIONS>  (5) 
1. Enzymatic Inhibition: Continuous FRET-based Mpro peptide cleavage assay (Dabcyl-KTSAVLQSGFRKME-Edans substrate); 2. Cellular Antiviral: SARS-CoV-2 cytopathic effect (CPE) inhibition and plaque reduction (PRNT50); 3. Microsomal Stability: Human liver microsomal (HLM) intrinsic clearance test without ritonavir co-factor.

